      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2590451972,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Thanks @johnthacker for all the work made on SSH dissector, there are no unnecessary expert_info now + dissection and decryption is working fine with year 2025 KEMs (using shared_secret)    \n\nFollowing your advice, I upgrade most of my SSH lab nodes to Trixie with libgcrypt 1.11.0 to work on private_key decryption (maybe some structural change would be needed as streamline NTRU and kyber key material are not bignum)",
